Documents](/site/assets/files/2122/002-file.svg)Supporting Documents](https://clinicalgenome.org/docs/?doc-type=supporting-documents#list_documentation_table)\n    -   [![Training Materials](/site/assets/files/2116/002-file.svg)Training Materials](https://clinicalgenome.org/docs/?doc-type=training-materials#list_documentation_table)\n    -   [![Website Updates](/site/assets/files/6235/002-file.svg)Website Updates](https://clinicalgenome.org/docs/?doc-type=website-updates#list_documentation_table)\n-   [Tools](https://clinicalgenome.org/tools/)\n\nGene\n\n-   Gene Symbol\n-   Gene Name\n-   Disease Name\n-   Drug Name\n-   Region (GRCh37)\n-   Region (GRCh38)\n\n-   [Variant](http://reg.clinicalgenome.org)\n-   [Website Content](https://clinicalgenome.org/search/)\n\n     Search\n\n-   [Curated Genes](https://search.clinicalgenome.org/kb/genes/curations)\n    -   [All Curated Genes](https://search.clinicalgenome.org/kb/genes/curations)\n    -   [ACMG SF v3.3 Curations](https://search.clinicalgenome.org/kb/genes/acmgsf)\n-   [Gene-Disease Validity](https://search.clinicalgenome.org/kb/gene-validity)\n    -   [All Curations](https://search.clinicalgenome.org/kb/gene-validity)\n    -   [Curations by Expert Panel](https://search.clinicalgenome.org/kb/affiliate)\n    \n    -   [File Downloads](https://search.clinicalgenome.org/kb/downloads/#section_gene-disease-validity')\n-   [Dosage Sensitivity](https://search.clinicalgenome.org/kb/gene-dosage)\n    -   [All Curations](https://search.clinicalgenome.org/kb/gene-dosage)\n    -   [Recurrent CNV](https://search.clinicalgenome.org/kb/gene-dosage/cnv)\n    \n    -   [FTP File Downloads (CSV, BED, TSV)](https://search.clinicalgenome.org/kb/downloads/#section_dosage')\n-   [Clinical Actionability](https://search.clinicalgenome.org/kb/actionability)\n    -   [All Curations](https://search.clinicalgenome.org/kb/actionability)\n    -   [Curations in Adult Context](https://actionability.clinicalgenome.org/ac/Adult/ui/summ)\n    -   [Curations in Pediatric Context](https://actionability.clinicalgenome.org/ac/Pediatric/ui/summ)\n    -   [Scoring Metric](https://www.clinicalgenome.org/docs/semi-quantitative-scoring-metric/)\n    \n    -   [File Downloads & APIs](https://search.clinicalgenome.org/kb/downloads/#section_actionability)\n-   [Curated Variants](https://search.clinicalgenome.org/kb/variant-pathogenicity/all)\n    -   [All Curations](https://search.clinicalgenome.org/kb/variant-pathogenicity/all)\n    \n    -   [File Downloads & APIs](https://search.clinicalgenome.org/kb/downloads#section_variant)\n-   [Statistics](https://search.clinicalgenome.org/kb/reports/stats)\n-   [More](#)\n    -   [All Genes](https://search.clinicalgenome.org/kb/genes)\n    -   [All Disease](https://search.clinicalgenome.org/kb/conditions)\n    -   [All Drugs & Medications](https://search.clinicalgenome.org/kb/drugs)\n    \n    -   [File Downloads & APIs](https://search.clinicalgenome.org/kb/downloads)\n-   [](#)\n    -   [About ClinGen's Website](/tools/clingen-website-faq/)\n    -   [Learn About New Features](/docs/?doc-type=website-updates)\n    -   [How To Cite ClinGen](/tools/clingen-website-faq/how-to-cite/)\n    -   [External Data Attribution](/tools/clingen-website-faq/attribution/)\n    -   [Contact Us](/about/contact-clingen/)\n\n# Clinical Domain Working Groups\n\n[Back](https://clinicalgenome.org/working-groups/clinical-domain/hereditary-cancer-cdwg/)\n\n## Childhood, Adolescent and Young Adult Cancer Predisposition Gene Curation Expert Panel\n\n[Affiliated to **Hereditary Cancer CDWG**](https://clinicalgenome.org/working-groups/clinical-domain/hereditary-cancer-cdwg/)\n\n[Membership](#heading_membership)\n\n---\n\nTechnological advances have led to increased understanding of the cancer predisposition disorders (CPDs) that result in an increased risk of childhood cancer. However, compared to adult cancers, establishing the clinical validity of genes for these disorders can prove challenging due to fewer studies, smaller sample sizes and a limited number of resources/databases focused on cancer risk in children and young adults. The Childhood, Adolescent and Young Adult Cancer Predisposition GCEP (CAYA GCEP) aims to curate and evaluate the gene-disease relationships (GDRs) primarily associated with these CPDs. The CAYA GCEP will review and initially curate 120 genes identified from OMIM, literature review and the hereditary gene panels used to assess cancer susceptibility by seven large pediatric institutions. While chosen for their association with CAYA, the GCEP will curate for all oncologic manifestations associated with a gene, regardless of age of onset. Among the identified, currently uncurated genes there is an enrichment of genes associated with predisposition to haematologic malignancies (HM) and so the CAYA GCEP will take a tiered approach starting first with 68 HM genes followed by 52 genes associated with CNS/solid tumours. The CAYA GCEP will include members from the Myeloid Malignancy VCEP, plans to work closely with the Hereditary Cancer GCEP and will collaborate with other GCEPs where there is an overlap. Thirteen genes from the gene list have a published ClinGen curation. For the genes where lumping and splitting shows a separate cancer predisposition assertion that has not been curated, these will either be treated as a split curation or a new GDR by our GCEP (depending on the evidence). We will also reach out to the relevant GCEPs to provide secondary contributions to curated syndromes.\n\nThe work of the CAYA GCEP will provide a critical foundation for the gene-disease associations in the CAYA oncology population, facilitating further refinement of hereditary cancer testing panels in clinical and cancer research.\n\n[View all Gene-Disease Validity classifications approved by this GCEP.](https://search.clinicalgenome.org/kb/affiliate/40157)\n\n#### Expert Panel Status *\\- Approved Expert Panel*\n\nStep 1\n\nStep 2\n\nDefine Group  \n*Complete*\n\nExpert Panel Approval  \n*Completed Jun. 2024*\n\n### Expert Panel Membership\n\nMembership spans many fields, including genetics, medical, academia, and industry.\n\n#### Chairs\n\n [![](/site/templates/resources/img/defaults/user_square.png ) **Noemi Fuentes Bolanos PhD**]( https://clinicalgenome.org/about/people/staff/fuentes-bolanos-12413 )\n\n [![](/site/templates/resources/img/defaults/user_square.png ) **Christopher Porter MD**]( https://clinicalgenome.org/about/people/staff/porter-12414 )\n\n [![](/site/templates/resources/img/defaults/user_square.png ) **Anita Villani MD**]( https://clinicalgenome.org/about/people/staff/villani-12412 )\n\n#### Coordinators\n\n [![](/site/assets/files/11372/pwimg_70c93h.600x600.png ) **Pamela Ajuyah Robertson PhD**]( https://clinicalgenome.org/about/people/staff/ajuyah-robertson-11372 )\n\n [![](/site/assets/files/11280/pwimg_opt2zh.600x600.png ) **Kelley Paris BS**]( https://clinicalgenome.org/about/people/staff/paris-11280 )\n\n#### [Members (57)](#collapseMembersmembershipAccordion14164)\n\n [![](/site/assets/files/11426/pwimg_tqq8sf.600x600.png ) **Yassmine Akkari, PhD**]( https://clinicalgenome.org/about/people/staff/akkari-11426 )\n\n [![](/site/assets/files/12418/pwimg_a11m0d.600x600.png ) **Ann Altekoester PhD**]( https://clinicalgenome.org/about/people/staff/altekoester-12418 )\n\n [![](/site/assets/files/12417/pwimg_6lgxde.600x600.png ) **Gabriel Bandeira MSc, PhD**]( https://clinicalgenome.org/about/people/staff/bandeira-12417 )\n\n [![](/site/templates/resources/img/defaults/user_square.png ) **Manoj Nepal CCRC PhD**]( https://clinicalgenome.org/about/people/staff/ccrc-12416 )\n\n [![](/site/assets/files/12435/pwimg_n29tnf.600x600.png ) **Vivian Chang MD**]( https://clinicalgenome.org/about/people/staff/chang-12435 )\n\n [![](/site/assets/files/12446/pwimg_j3yp6e.600x600.png ) **Eliza Courtney MGC, BSc (Hons), FHGSA**]( https://clinicalgenome.org/about/people/staff/courtney-12446 )\n\n [![](/site/assets/file